                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As far as platformers go, this game is brutally hard, and asks a lot from the player. That is the most important thing to consider before picking it up.\n\nDeceptively simple, the game has only a handful of mechanics, but it combines them in every conceivable way. Every possible trial and tribulation will be brought forward for you to face, and you best be prepared to spend a long, long time mastering it before you see the end of the game.\n\nThe game at times suffers from a lack of direction, not in terms of design, but in terms of not telling the player where to go. This is frustrating, and there aren't guides out there for the game to inform you of what to do next. I spent a good hour trying to figure out where to go after the Hospital segment, only to discover that the game had activated an extra teleporter without ever informing me of it. That was quite frustrating. But ultimately did not take away from the experience enough to justify a negative review.\n\nI think this paticular title could have done with some extra beta testing, that would likely have smoothed a few of the edges out.\n\nI will give a special shoutout to the music, which is absolutely phenomenal in this title, each new area brought with it an absolute bop of a soundtrack.\n\nAll in all, this game is worth playing if you love hard platformers, being challenged, or are a sadist.",
